Subject: [PATCH] modelblaster: Moonshine's encoder in the int8 FX path, and the kernels it needs

ROCC_DECOUPLED.md 7.8 recorded that Moonshine Tiny could not be code-generated at all:
the int8 extractor had no tanh_s8, no groupnorm_s8, no rotary embedding, refused
view/reshape/permute, and lowered a multi-head scaled_dot_product_attention to ONE
attention over every head's rows -- the wrong function, silently.  This patch makes the
encoder (fpga/pynq-z2/modelblaster/moonshine/moonshine_enc.py, bit-identical to
transformers' MoonshineEncoder in float32) extract, simulate and code-generate.
Curated kernels live OUTSIDE the submodule, at fpga/pynq-z2/modelblaster/kernels/, reached
with --global-curated-dir as patches/0009 and 0060 arranged.

1. pipeline/extract_graph.py -- the FX int8 path.
   * tanh (nn.Tanh, torch.tanh, F.tanh) -> tanh_s8.
   * nn.GroupNorm(num_groups=1) over [N,C,L] / [N,C,H,W] -> groupnorm_s8 (per-channel
     gamma/beta); more groups refuses.
   * A model's rotary-embedding LEAF -> one rope_s8 dispatch.  Modules declaring
     `mb_fx_leaf = True` are traced whole (_MbLeafTracer); a model declaring none takes
     torch.fx.symbolic_trace itself, so every existing graph traces identically.  rope_s8
     is recognised by `mb_op == "rope_s8"`, INTERLEAVED pairing only (anything else
     refuses), cos/sin tables [T, R/2] from the module (the model's own inv_freq), shared
     between instances through `mb_table_key`.
   * view / reshape / contiguous / flatten -> view.  permute / transpose -> view when only
     unit axes move, else permute4_s8 (a COPY; scale carried through).
   * MULTI-HEAD sdpa ([B, heads, S, D], heads > 1): matmul_b_s8 (Q.K^T per head) ->
     softmax_s8 (B*heads*S rows) -> matmul_b_s8 (probs.V per head), with the attention
     score scale CALIBRATED from q.k recomputed on every calibration sample.  The
     single-head decomposition is untouched.
   * Golden simulator: C-exact simulation of the new ops (float32 where the C is float32,
     sequential double sums where the C sums sequentially, roundf half-away).
     MB_INT8_GOLDEN_C_FLOAT=1 extends that to add_s8, mul_s8, softmax_s8, matmul_s8,
     gelu_s8 and layernorm_s8, whose default simulation is float64 / pairwise-summed /
     np.round half-even and disagrees with the reference kernels by an LSB once a graph has
     millions of elements (5.8 M attention scores here).  OFF by default.
   * MB_INT8_GELU_AWARE_RANGES=1: a tensor whose every consumer is an exact GELU is
     calibrated to max(positive max, min(negative max, 8)) -- GELU(x <= -8) is 0 to
     1e-15, so saturating that tail loses nothing.  Moonshine's stem conv3 spans -1,390 ..
     +29; stock max-abs left GELU a handful of codes.  OFF by default.
   * MB_INT8_DUMP_ACTIVATIONS=<npz>: every simulated tensor, for per-dispatch host gates.
   * _sim_conv2d_s8 / _sim_conv2d_int32_acc: the per-element Python loop replaced by one
     exact int64 matrix product (hours -> a second on Moonshine's stem).  Same integers.

2. pipeline/reference_kernels.py -- KernelSpecs tanh_s8, groupnorm_s8, rope_s8 (references
   in gelu_s8's, layernorm_s8's and mul_s8's float shapes), and AlgorithmCandidates:
     tanh_s8     pext_memo_lut    pext, pext_nl  BIT_EXACT (256-entry memo of tanhf)
     add_s8      pext_int_add     pext_nl        BIT_EXACT, no float instruction
     mul_s8      pext_int_mul     pext_nl        BIT_EXACT, no float instruction
     rope_s8     pext_int_rot     pext_nl        BIT_EXACT, no float instruction
     matmul_b_s8 pext_dot8_exact  pext_nl        BIT_EXACT, DOT8 reduction for any K
     groupnorm_s8 pext_int_rsqrt  pext_nl        NUMERIC_DRIFT (1 LSB)
   The integer add / mul / rope / matmul tail are exact because a fixed-point fast path is
   used only outside a proven bound on the reference's float32 rounding error; inside it
   the element is evaluated in exact IEEE-754 binary32 arithmetic on integers
   (fpga/pynq-z2/sw/fexact32.h).  Checked by fpga/pynq-z2/modelblaster/moonshine/
   check_moonshine.py over every int8 operand pair at thousands of scale triples, ASan +
   UBSan, and every dispatch of Moonshine's encoder on its golden input.
   With this patch pext_nl codegen of ffn_block picks pext_int_add and attn_block picks
   pext_int_mul (both bit-exact); on `pext` nothing changes.

3. pipeline/generate_skeleton.py -- call emitters for tanh_s8, groupnorm_s8, rope_s8
   (permute4_s8 and matmul_b_s8 already had them).

4. pipeline/generate_kernels.py -- --keep-reference-ops was a silent no-op for any op
   kind with a curated kernel on the target: the curated PRE-SEED wrote the curated source
   into impls before _probe_swap consulted the pin, and kernel_picks.json still reported
   "reference".  Pinned kinds are no longer pre-seeded.

5. pipeline/verify_kernel.py -- host verify input generators / runners for tanh_s8,
   groupnorm_s8, rope_s8.

6. models/moonshine_enc.py, moonshine_stem_w.py, moonshine_stem_h.py -- shims into
   $IISWC_ROOT/fpga/pynq-z2/modelblaster/moonshine/ (weights fetched, not committed).

Checked: ffn_block, attn_block, norm_block (1 calibration sample), kws_digit_ctc_t (64),
lenet, dronet, kws_cnn (4) extract to byte-identical graph.json / io.npz / weights.npz
before and after this patch, and their `pext` codegen is identical.

Applied by scripts/50_rocket_moonshine_enc.sh.  Depends on patches/0009 and 0060 (0020 and
0070 may be applied too).  NOT upstream.

